00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:08.190 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  Marvel vs. Capcom Infinite has moved  away from three character fights in  favor of a two-player tag anywhere any  time system that puts an entirely new  spin on your team synergy now if you'd  like to see some gameplay of that you  can check out the livestream that you're  at and I did last week where I swag on  him just a little but the game also  introduces or reintroduces rather if you  remember the Marvel Super Heroes game  from 1985 the six Infinity stones in the  Marvel Universe now each one grants your  character a move that they can perform  at any time during the match called in  infinity surge as well as a super  powerful ability that effectively breaks  the game for a while and that's the  Infinity storm and this leaves room for  near infinite possibilities with team  composition as your two characters will  have very different strategies depending  on which infinity stone you pick so if  you're eager to jump in and start  bodying people right away we've got you  covered we're going to take a look at  each stone what they can do and  suggestions for characters or strategies  that you should use with them  [Music]  speeding its way into the first slot on  our list the time stone offers your  characters a quick teleport and dash  ability that you can use to close the  distance between you and your opponents  or create some devious and mix ups you  might want to use a stone if your  character lacks mobility options so  people who can't fly can't air - this  might be perfect for them activating  time stones in fancy storms speeds you  up significantly and gives your  characters some nasty custom combo  abilities basically your moves now have  zero recovery time and they can all link  into each other so if you ever want to  do a combo with twenty hard kicks in a  row now's your chance as long as your  characters have normals that move them  forward slightly you'll be able to carry  them all the way to the corner with this  stone if what you're looking for is some  zoning assistance to help you out in  your neutral the reality stone might be  for you using the Infinity surge tosses  out a slow-moving projectile that homes  in on your opponent it's good for  creating space and can be super annoying  to deal with so giving it's characters  that lacks a zoning abilities is a good  option or you can just use it with an  already projectile heavy character like  zero or Dormammu for added pressure and  before you snap back to reality  make sure you use the Infinity storm  which spits out massive elemental  attacks with every normal move you  perform light punch shoots out little  bolts of energy like kick freezes  opponents hard punch charges up a huge  beam of fire and hard kick summons a  pillar of electricity all the attacks  are great for cover while you rush down  and it can easily catch opponents who  try to run away from you while the  infinity storm is active also one thing  to note is that you can only send out  one elemental attack at a time but that  limitation is per character so what you  want to do is send down an attack tag in  your character and then you can have two  of them on screen at once  allowing you to use them for some pretty  wicked combos  the mind is a terrible thing to waste  and the mind stone is no different you  don't want to waste any opportunities to  use the stones surged ability as they'll  perform a grab which then leaves your  opponent dizzy for a few seconds and as  for the infinity storm the mind stone  causes your team to constantly regain  meter throughout its duration now this  is great for all characters but  especially those with powerup hyper  combos like X or firebrand and  characters with hyper combos that  persist on the screen like Dormammu and  Rocket Raccoon just make sure to use  your meter you don't want to be at four  bars while the infinity storm is still  going and then you just waste all that  meter I'm sad to report that this stone  does not in fact launch an awesome 4  player 3d re umbrella at the opponent  but instead using the infinity surge  throws out a short-range attack that  causes a wall bounce you can use this as  a combo extension or as a powerful  anti-air tool and it's a great stone to  start out with while you learn how the  combo system works as the Infinity storm  doesn't actually change your play too  much well other than the fact that your  attacks will do a ton more damage and  cause gigantic wall bounces so if you  like piling the hurt onto your  opponent's the power stone is definitely  the way to go  [Music]  as far as toying with your opponents go  the space stone has a lot to offer using  the stones infinity search pulls the  player towards you  not unlike Magneto and storms moves in  Marvel 3 but since you can cancel the  surge with the hyper combo characters  with grab supers will probably benefit  from the stone the most got a pesky  spider-man playing keep-away with you  pull them in and smash their puny little  spider bits to pieces  the stones infinity storm otherwise  known as putting them in a box traps the  opponent in this little enclosure and  gives them few ways to defend themselves  they can't switch characters or even  move beyond the confines of the box it  effectively creates a corner for  yourself so think about using characters  that can utilize some quick high-low  mix-ups or characters with teleports  like Dante or even stick with your big  body team and command grab them today  they've got nowhere to go so let's make  them comfy with a nice piledriver  the mayor  and finally to cap off this madness we  have the soul stone it's not too  impressive at first with an infinity  surge that does a quick but low damaging  life drain but hold on to your butts  because once you've build enough meter  it offers one of the craziest abilities  ever seen in the Marvel vs. Capcom  series you know how when your character  dies they just kind of stay on the  screen instead of vanishing into thin  air like previous games  well the infinity storm for this puppy  brings that character back to life with  15% health and echoing the Street  Fighter Alpha dramatic valves and that  one glitch for Marvel 3 allows you to  control both characters on screen at the  same time if you're unsure if this game  could rival the insanity of previous  Marvel games this is all the proof that  you need right here the soul stone opens  the floodgates for an entirely new set  of combos to style on someone with and  really hammers home the infinite in the  game's title now you don't have to wait  until one of your character dies but  being able to revive them puts a lot of  pressure on your opponent to think twice  about when to kill you your movement and  button inputs will be identical for both  characters so you'll probably need to  spend a lot of time in training mode  trying to figure out which moves to  perform and when but really it all  depends on what characters you pick  characters with teleports projectiles  and good rushdown abilities will do  really well with the stone Dormammu for  example is a great partner to have with  this as he can easily charge up his  powers while hyper combos going on in  the foreground allowing you to rain  Hellfire afterwards  so those are all six at the Infinity  stones in Marvel vs. Capcom infinite  there's also one more thing that applies  to all the stones and that's the fact  that only one infinity storm can be  active at a time so you'll need to be  smart about when you use it for example  if your opponent has the soul stone and  you just know that they're about to  revive their second character you can  activate your own infinity storm to  block the theirs but that's just one  small part of the meadow there's still  tons of tech to discover and this video  is just a primer so get into that  training room and putting some work now  if you have any strats or team comps  that everyone should be aware of don't  save it for Evo just put it in the  comments below and don't forget to check  out the review of the game on GameSpot  calm while you're at it  my name is Joey and thanks for watching

